    "reading": "Every file tqwebp writes decodes in libwebp, which is the browser decoder. On the photo class the two measurements agree to 0.0000 dB, which pins the colour convention end to end. On flat art and screenshots libwebp reports up to 1.32 dB more, because libwebp upsamples chroma with a bilinear filter and golang.org/x/image repeats each chroma sample. The oracle therefore reads slightly low on hard colour edges, never high, so every gate number in this repository is conservative.",
